 prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record from 1951 to 2025 shows November to December came in under 90% of normal in 36 of 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids. On that same middle, 2025 ran dry late, with August to September at 47% of normal and September to October at 38% of normal in 2025. In 2026, June to July came in at 150% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 25654 had its driest year in 1988, at 55% of normal.</p>"}
